{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011MvxzaErxD7nJgn44aXAQW","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"repo\":\"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core\",\"number\":1905,\"kind\":\"pr\",\"title\":\"(docs) Rewrite the openmrs CLI README around how it's used\",\"state\":\"merged\",\"author\":\"denniskigen\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-09-27T20:12:59.000Z\",\"mergedAt\":\"2026-10-02T15:01:58.000Z\",\"closedAt\":\"2026-10-02T15:01:58.000Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/pull/1905\",\"mergeCommit\":\"b439966ee59c5a9d0cc569942c6fb6d98bb28ba4\",\"syncedAt\":\"2026-10-31T16:11:06.195Z\",\"tickets\":[],\"commits\":[{\"sha\":\"b439966ee59c5a9d0cc569942c6fb6d98bb28ba4\",\"source\":\"merge-commit-sha\",\"verified\":true}],\"files\":[{\"path\":\".changeset/cli-readme-rewrite.md\",\"additions\":5,\"deletions\":0},{\"path\":\"packages/tooling/openmrs/README.md\",\"additions\":202,\"deletions\":35},{\"path\":\"packages/tooling/openmrs/src/cli.ts\",\"additions\":12,\"deletions\":9}],\"body\":\"## Requirements\\n\\n- [x] This PR has a title that briefly describes the work done including the ticket number. If there is a ticket, make sure your PR title includes a [conventional commit](https://o3-docs.openmrs.org/en-US/docs/frontend-modules/contributing/#contributing-guidelines) label. See existing PR titles for inspiration.\\n- [ ] My work is based on designs, which are linked or shown either in the Jira ticket or the description below. (See also: [Styleguide](http://om.rs/o3ui))\\n- [x] My work includes tests or is validated by existing tests.\\n- [ ] I have updated the esm-framework and storybook mocks ([mock.tsx](https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/blob/main/packages/framework/esm-framework/mock.tsx), [mock-jest.tsx](https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/blob/main/packages/framework/esm-framework/mock-jest.tsx), and [storybook mocks](https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/blob/main/packages/tooling/storybook/mocks/)) to reflect any API changes.\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nThe `openmrs` README only listed the four commands with a one-line example each, so most of what the CLI does wasn't written down anywhere. This rewrites it around the three places it's used:\\n\\n- developing a frontend module with `openmrs develop`\\n- building a distribution with `openmrs assemble` and `openmrs build`\\n- the `rspack` and `webpack` commands and shared configs that modules build with\\n\\nEach section covers the options, the config file formats, and the behaviour that's easy to miss. For example, `build --fresh` also deletes what `assemble` wrote, the build config wins over flags except for `importmap`, `routes` and `defaultLocale`, and the default `importmap` and `routes` URLs are relative to the current page. It also links to the reference application's setup for serving the compressed copies and for filling in per-deployment settings with `envsubst`.\\n\\nA couple of current limitations are called out directly: `assets` in the build config is ignored, and relative local paths in the build config aren't resolved against the working directory. Those notes can come out when the fixes land.\\n\\nThe `--help` epilog had drifted as well. It said `configPaths` and `configUrls` are comma-separated (they're JSON arrays), described `spa-assemble-config.json` as the file both commands read, and was missing `routes`, `defaultLocale`, `env` and `frontendModuleExcludes`. It now matches the code and links to the README.\\n\\n## Screenshots\\n\\n## Related Issue\\n\\n## Other\\n\\nI checked what the README says against the code, and ran the CLI for the behaviour that was easy to get wrong, like `--fresh`.\\n\\nOffline support (`--support-offline` and `supportOffline`) is left out, since #1894 removed it.\",\"freshness\":[{\"repo\":\"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core\",\"lastSyncedAt\":\"2026-10-31T16:11:06.195Z\",\"stale\":false}],\"nextOffset\":null,\"truncated\":[]}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use