{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011MqohaKXssqFPQC18CEdPr","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"repo\":\"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core\",\"number\":1838,\"kind\":\"pr\",\"title\":\"(feat) O3-5872: Add support for static compression of frontend\",\"state\":\"merged\",\"author\":\"ibacher\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-08-06T21:08:05.000Z\",\"mergedAt\":\"2026-08-07T17:46:53.000Z\",\"closedAt\":\"2026-08-07T17:46:53.000Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/pull/1838\",\"mergeCommit\":\"16a6c01d099267045f174f95ecf3936d3b770fb9\",\"syncedAt\":\"2026-10-31T16:11:06.195Z\",\"tickets\":[{\"key\":\"O3-5872\",\"source\":\"ticket-pattern\"}],\"commits\":[{\"sha\":\"16a6c01d099267045f174f95ecf3936d3b770fb9\",\"source\":\"merge-commit-sha\",\"verified\":true}],\"files\":[{\"path\":\".changeset/all-spiders-bet.md\",\"additions\":5,\"deletions\":0},{\"path\":\"packages/tooling/openmrs/src/cli.test.ts\",\"additions\":13,\"deletions\":0},{\"path\":\"packages/tooling/openmrs/src/cli.ts\",\"additions\":20,\"deletions\":2},{\"path\":\"packages/tooling/openmrs/src/commands/build.integration.test.ts\",\"additions\":43,\"deletions\":1},{\"path\":\"packages/tooling/openmrs/src/commands/build.ts\",\"additions\":24,\"deletions\":2},{\"path\":\"packages/tooling/openmrs/src/utils/compress.test.ts\",\"additions\":472,\"deletions\":0},{\"path\":\"packages/tooling/openmrs/src/utils/compress.ts\",\"additions\":479,\"deletions\":0},{\"path\":\"packages/tooling/openmrs/src/utils/index.ts\",\"additions\":1,\"deletions\":0}],\"body\":\"## Requirements\\r\\n\\r\\n- [x] This PR has a title that briefly describes the work done including the ticket number. If there is a ticket, make sure your PR title includes a [conventional commit](https://o3-docs.openmrs.org/en-US/docs/frontend-modules/contributing/#contributing-guidelines) label. See existing PR titles for inspiration.\\r\\n- [ ] My work is based on designs, which are linked or shown either in the Jira ticket or the description below. (See also: [Styleguide](http://om.rs/o3ui))\\r\\n- [x] My work includes tests or is validated by existing tests.\\r\\n- [ ] I have updated the esm-framework and storybook mocks ([mock.tsx](https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/blob/main/packages/framework/esm-framework/mock.tsx), [mock-jest.tsx](https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/blob/main/packages/framework/esm-framework/mock-jest.tsx), and [storybook mocks](https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/blob/main/packages/tooling/storybook/mocks/)) to reflect any API changes.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Summary\\r\\n<!-- Please describe what problems your PR addresses. -->\\r\\n\\r\\nThis adds a few options to the `build` subcommand of the `openmrs` CLI to automatically generate pre-compressed versions of all `.js`, `.mjs`, `.cjs`, `.css`, `.json`, `.svg`, `.html`, and `.map` files if compressing the file will save disk space.\\r\\n\\r\\nCurrently, in the RefApp and module-spa, we serve most files using real-time gzip compression, meaning the server applies gzip compression for each request. This wastes CPU cycles since the files served themselves are static. Additionally, because this is done on-the-fly, the level of compression applied is minimal (equivalent to `gzip -1`). Additionally, we miss out on [Brotli](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brotli) compression, which is supported by all major browsers and generally provides better compression ratios than gzip for web assets. \\r\\n\\r\\nCompressed artifacts are on by default with the `build` command but can be turned _off_ by passing `--no-compress`. Similarly, specific versions can be turned off by `--no-compress-brotli` or `--no-compress-gzip`. This applies the maximum level of both gzip and brotli compression.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis PR is designed to output files in a format that can be consumed, without modification, by nginx's `gzip_static` directive and a future PR will add a similar implementation to module-spa, allowing us to serve frontend assets in smaller bundles.\\r\\n\\r\\nFor the Reference Application, there are 12.7 MB of assets on disk and compressed these become 2.4 MB (gzip) or 1.9 MB (brotli). Note, though that with both nginx and module-spa, we do gzip compress by default, but these numbers still compare favorably to the current size of 2.9 MB for all assets using the lowest level of gzip compression.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Screenshots\\r\\n<!-- Required if you are making UI changes. -->\\r\\n\\r\\n## Related Issue\\r\\n<!-- Paste the link to the Jira ticket here if one exists. -->\\r\\n<!-- https://issues.openmrs.org/browse/O3- -->\\r\\n\\r\\n## Other\\r\\n<!-- Anything not covered above -->\\r\\n\\r\\n### Second Opinion\\r\\n\\r\\nOne thing I could use a second opinion on: the code will in some cases automatically \\\"clean-up\\\" after itself, e.g., if `file1.js` in one version compresses well, so that `file1.js.gz` and `file1.js.br` are generated, but then `file1.js` is changed so that it doesn't compress well (or is under the 1 kB minimum for compression to be applied), the `file1.js.gz` and `file1.js.br` files will be automatically removed on the next build. However, if you run `openmrs build` or `openmrs build --compress` and later run `openmrs build --no-compress-brotli`, the code will not automatically delete any existing `file1.js.br` files. I _think_ this makes the result more intuitive, but I'm not completely sold.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf I didn't explain this well, see Copliot's comment [here](https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/pull/1838#discussion_r3731915835) which is the same thing.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Notes on the ticket\\r\\n\\r\\nThe ticket initially specified that this compression should be added to the `assemble` step, but since `openmrs build` is run _after_ assemble (to be able to correctly identify the `importmap.json` and `routes.registry.json` files if those have been content-hashed), that meant that the app shell's own code was never compressed and `openmrs.css` is the largest single file in the RefApp frontend (and likely every other distribution), so this was re-targeted at the `build` step. Obviously, if we change that back for some reason, we would also need to change this.\",\"freshness\":[{\"repo\":\"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core\",\"lastSyncedAt\":\"2026-10-31T16:11:06.195Z\",\"stale\":false}],\"nextOffset\":null,\"truncated\":[]}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7037fe60-7ca4-4a10-bd8f-9455884bf9b1","uuid":"ec01bf05-f069-4a46-8f46-fdb8514a1f08","timestamp":"2026-10-31T16:23:48.872Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"repo\":\"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core\",\"number\":1838,\"kind\":\"pr\",\"title\":\"(feat) O3-5872: Add support for static compression of frontend\",\"state\":\"merged\",\"author\":\"ibacher\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-08-06T21:08:05.000Z\",\"mergedAt\":\"2026-08-07T17:46:53.000Z\",\"closedAt\":\"2026-08-07T17:46:53.000Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/pull/1838\",\"mergeCommit\":\"16a6c01d099267045f174f95ecf3936d3b770fb9\",\"syncedAt\":\"2026-10-31T16:11:06.195Z\",\"tickets\":[{\"key\":\"O3-5872\",\"source\":\"ticket-pattern\"}],\"commits\":[{\"sha\":\"16a6c01d099267045f174f95ecf3936d3b770fb9\",\"source\":\"merge-commit-sha\",\"verified\":true}],\"files\":[{\"path\":\".changeset/all-spiders-bet.md\",\"additions\":5,\"deletions\":0},{\"path\":\"packages/tooling/openmrs/src/cli.test.ts\",\"additions\":13,\"deletions\":0},{\"path\":\"packages/tooling/openmrs/src/cli.ts\",\"additions\":20,\"deletions\":2},{\"path\":\"packages/tooling/openmrs/src/commands/build.integration.test.ts\",\"additions\":43,\"deletions\":1},{\"path\":\"packages/tooling/openmrs/src/commands/build.ts\",\"additions\":24,\"deletions\":2},{\"path\":\"packages/tooling/openmrs/src/utils/compress.test.ts\",\"additions\":472,\"deletions\":0},{\"path\":\"packages/tooling/openmrs/src/utils/compress.ts\",\"additions\":479,\"deletions\":0},{\"path\":\"packages/tooling/openmrs/src/utils/index.ts\",\"additions\":1,\"deletions\":0}],\"body\":\"## Requirements\\r\\n\\r\\n- [x] This PR has a title that briefly describes the work done including the ticket number. If there is a ticket, make sure your PR title includes a [conventional commit](https://o3-docs.openmrs.org/en-US/docs/frontend-modules/contributing/#contributing-guidelines) label. See existing PR titles for inspiration.\\r\\n- [ ] My work is based on designs, which are linked or shown either in the Jira ticket or the description below. (See also: [Styleguide](http://om.rs/o3ui))\\r\\n- [x] My work includes tests or is validated by existing tests.\\r\\n- [ ] I have updated the esm-framework and storybook mocks ([mock.tsx](https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/blob/main/packages/framework/esm-framework/mock.tsx), [mock-jest.tsx](https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/blob/main/packages/framework/esm-framework/mock-jest.tsx), and [storybook mocks](https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/blob/main/packages/tooling/storybook/mocks/)) to reflect any API changes.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Summary\\r\\n<!-- Please describe what problems your PR addresses. -->\\r\\n\\r\\nThis adds a few options to the `build` subcommand of the `openmrs` CLI to automatically generate pre-compressed versions of all `.js`, `.mjs`, `.cjs`, `.css`, `.json`, `.svg`, `.html`, and `.map` files if compressing the file will save disk space.\\r\\n\\r\\nCurrently, in the RefApp and module-spa, we serve most files using real-time gzip compression, meaning the server applies gzip compression for each request. This wastes CPU cycles since the files served themselves are static. Additionally, because this is done on-the-fly, the level of compression applied is minimal (equivalent to `gzip -1`). Additionally, we miss out on [Brotli](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brotli) compression, which is supported by all major browsers and generally provides better compression ratios than gzip for web assets. \\r\\n\\r\\nCompressed artifacts are on by default with the `build` command but can be turned _off_ by passing `--no-compress`. Similarly, specific versions can be turned off by `--no-compress-brotli` or `--no-compress-gzip`. This applies the maximum level of both gzip and brotli compression.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis PR is designed to output files in a format that can be consumed, without modification, by nginx's `gzip_static` directive and a future PR will add a similar implementation to module-spa, allowing us to serve frontend assets in smaller bundles.\\r\\n\\r\\nFor the Reference Application, there are 12.7 MB of assets on disk and compressed these become 2.4 MB (gzip) or 1.9 MB (brotli). Note, though that with both nginx and module-spa, we do gzip compress by default, but these numbers still compare favorably to the current size of 2.9 MB for all assets using the lowest level of gzip compression.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Screenshots\\r\\n<!-- Required if you are making UI changes. -->\\r\\n\\r\\n## Related Issue\\r\\n<!-- Paste the link to the Jira ticket here if one exists. -->\\r\\n<!-- https://issues.openmrs.org/browse/O3- -->\\r\\n\\r\\n## Other\\r\\n<!-- Anything not covered above -->\\r\\n\\r\\n### Second Opinion\\r\\n\\r\\nOne thing I could use a second opinion on: the code will in some cases automatically \\\"clean-up\\\" after itself, e.g., if `file1.js` in one version compresses well, so that `file1.js.gz` and `file1.js.br` are generated, but then `file1.js` is changed so that it doesn't compress well (or is under the 1 kB minimum for compression to be applied), the `file1.js.gz` and `file1.js.br` files will be automatically removed on the next build. However, if you run `openmrs build` or `openmrs build --compress` and later run `openmrs build --no-compress-brotli`, the code will not automatically delete any existing `file1.js.br` files. I _think_ this makes the result more intuitive, but I'm not completely sold.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf I didn't explain this well, see Copliot's comment [here](https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core/pull/1838#discussion_r3731915835) which is the same thing.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Notes on the ticket\\r\\n\\r\\nThe ticket initially specified that this compression should be added to the `assemble` step, but since `openmrs build` is run _after_ assemble (to be able to correctly identify the `importmap.json` and `routes.registry.json` files if those have been content-hashed), that meant that the app shell's own code was never compressed and `openmrs.css` is the largest single file in the RefApp frontend (and likely every other distribution), so this was re-targeted at the `build` step. Obviously, if we change that back for some reason, we would also need to change this.\",\"freshness\":[{\"repo\":\"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core\",\"lastSyncedAt\":\"2026-10-31T16:11:06.195Z\",\"stale\":false}],\"nextOffset\":null,\"truncated\":[]}"}],"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_011MqohaKXssqFPQC18CEdPr","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
